## [0.4.2] - 2026-02-14

### Added
- **Aspire AppHost Integration**: New GRRADO.AppHost project for unified backend debugging
  - Orchestrates all 8 .NET services (API Gateway + 7 microservices) from single entry point
  - Provides Aspire Dashboard (http://localhost:18888) for real-time monitoring
  - Services run with fixed ports: Gateway 5100, Services 5101-5107
  - Health check endpoints on all services (`/health`) for Aspire integration
  - Gateway references all services via Aspire for service discovery
- **Aspire Documentation**: Comprehensive guide in docs/00-getting-started/04-aspire-debugging.md
  - Setup instructions (F5 debugging, CLI launch)
  - Dashboard usage guide (logs, traces, endpoints)
  - Service endpoints reference table
  - Troubleshooting guide for common issues
  - Workflow examples and comparison with docker-compose-only approach

### Changed
- Updated all 7 microservice Program.cs files to add health checks
- UserService, VehicleService, GarageService, ServiceHistoryService, ChatbotService, DiagnosticsService, LoggingService now import HealthChecks
- Added `builder.Services.AddHealthChecks()` and `app.MapHealthChecks("/health")` to all services
- ApiGateway already had health checks, no changes needed

### Architecture
- **Local Development**: Docker-compose for infrastructure (PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, Keycloak) + Aspire for .NET services
- **Clean Separation**: Stateless services orchestrated by Aspire, stateful infrastructure via docker-compose
- **No Breaking Changes**: Existing service code patterns unchanged, only added health checks and Aspire compatibility
- **Unified Experience**: F5 in VS Code now launches all services with dashboard

### Deployment
- Aspire AppHost is development-only tool
- Production uses docker-compose for full orchestration (future: add service containers to docker-compose.yml)
- Solution maintains compatibility with docker-compose-only deployment on CI/CD

### Version Bump
**Version:** 0.4.2 (feature release)
**Reason:** Added Aspire AppHost for improved local debugging experience, zero impact on production deployment
